{
 "encounter_id": "00947",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
  "person_4": "CLINICAL_STAFF"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good afternoon, Mr Doyle, Mrs Doyle. The booking says inhaler technique review. What's been happening? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Well, the breathing, you know. Not good. A bit all over the place."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Can you say more? When are you breathless?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Going up the hill to the shops. Or, I don't know, sometimes sitting."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Not sitting, Tom. When you hurry. And he coughs all the time, doctor, morning mostly."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And does he wheeze?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "At night, yes. I can hear it from my side of the bed."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any chest pain?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No pain, no."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Fever?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No fever."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Coughing up blood?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No blood."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Swollen ankles?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "No, his ankles are fine."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Weight loss?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "No, if anything he's put on a bit."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And which inhalers do you use at the moment, Tom?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "The blue one. The puffer. I can't remember what it's called. The blue one, for when I'm wheezy."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_4",
   "t": "It's in his bag, doctor, I can read it for you later, but I think the label's worn off."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's fine, we'll find it on the record. Any allergies to medicines?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No allergies."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What conditions have you got?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Asthma, since I was a boy. And hay fever."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any operations?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Tonsils, as a lad. And a hernia in 2012."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Asthma in the family?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My mother had it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you smoke?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I stopped smoking ten years ago."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And what did you do for work?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "He was a postman, thirty years. Retired."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you get out walking?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "When I can. The dog needs it more than me."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check you. Pulse 84, blood pressure 140 over 86, temperature 36.7, oxygen 94 percent, breathing 18, weight 80 kilos.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Is the oxygen all right? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "A bit lower than I'd like, but not alarming. Let me listen. Big breaths, Tom.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Like this? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I can hear wheeze on both sides, mostly when you breathe out."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "That's the whistle. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And your chest is moving well, with no signs of struggling. Your heart sounds are normal."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "That's good. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any palpitations, any trouble with your heart?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, nothing at all."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any heartburn or trouble swallowing?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, nothing. I eat like a horse."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Now I'd like to see how you use the blue puffer. Priya, would you hand him the demonstration one? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_4",
   "t": "Of course. Here you are, Mr Doyle. Breathe out first, then press, and breathe in slowly. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Like that? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_4",
   "t": "You pressed, and then you breathed in too fast, and held it for just a second. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's the common problem. The medicine is hitting the back of your throat instead of the lungs. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "So it's not working? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Not as well as it could. I think the poor technique is limiting the benefit of the inhaler."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Oh dear. I've been doing it wrong for years. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It's very common, you're not alone. I'd like to start tiotropium, 18 micrograms, once a day, from a different type of inhaler, and a budesonide inhaler, 200 micrograms, twice a day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Will he need a spacer? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_4",
   "t": "I'll show you both devices and a spacer, Mrs Doyle. They make it much easier. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you, Priya. I'd also like to arrange spirometry, to measure your breathing properly, and a chest X-ray."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "When? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "This month. And I'd like to see you again in four weeks to see how the new inhalers are doing."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Four weeks. We'll write it on the calendar. ~"
  }
 ],
